\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thy ceaseless, unexhausted love, 
\par Unmerited and free
\par Delights our evil to remove, 
\par And help our misery.
\par   \tab 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thou waitest to be gracious still;
\par Thou dost with sinners bear, 
\par That, saved, we may Thy goodness feel,
\par And all Thy grace declare.
\par  
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thy goodness and Thy truth to me,
\par To every soul, abound, 
\par A vast, unfathomable sea,
\par Where all our thoughts are drowned.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Its streams the whole creation reach,
\par So plenteous is the store,
\par Enough for all, enough for each,
\par Enough forever more. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Faithful, O Lord, Thy mercies are, 
\par A rock that cannot move:
\par A thousand promises declare 
\par Thy constancy of love. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Throughout the universe it reigns, 
\par Unalterably sure;\tab 
\par And while the truth of God remains, 
\par The goodness must endure. 
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

